 The [per-track tuning API](app/instrument.h) supports custom tuning; a dedicated tuning editor is not included.
 
+## Operator waveforms (open web engine)
+
+The browser simulator's DX7 engine (`web/synth`) has an opsix-style per-operator waveform: sine (default, bit-exact with the original), triangle, saw, square, half-wave sine and full-wave sine. Set it with the `sim_op_wave(track, op, wave)` export (`op` 0-5 = panel OP1-OP6, `wave` 0-5, or -1 to read back). It is a live timbre control: it is not saved in projects and resets when the track's source is reset. Hard-edged waves are not band-limited and alias at high pitches. This is a web-simulator feature only; the device engine is the binary SDK and is unchanged.
+
+Run `tools/test_opwaves.sh` (clang and git on Linux/macOS) to check the waveforms, the bit-exact sine path against the original core, and the full simulator wiring.
